text+=['','Each entry in [the final register]('+str(register)+') retains exact original IDs, source lines, required capabilities, sequence, proof status, disagreements, remedy and re-audit property. Historical review IDs and statuses remain in the separately sealed [historical comparison]('+str(O/'HISTORICAL-COMPARISON.md')+'); historical acceptance claims are not current user acceptance.','','## Evidence and disagreement','','RF-001 concerns the economic relationship between prize delivery and independently payable proceeds under the explicit untrusted-prize DESIGN scope. Honest continuously transferable ERC721 semantics, dishonest ownership reports and later transfer refusal are distinct cases within that conditional root family. Exact quote accounting can hold while promised economic delivery fails. RF-002 is the narrow sponsor-selected future-clone recipient case, with an actual honest-ERC721 reproduction; it is own-recipient loss under strict setup, not general EOA theft. The register preserves conditional High/Medium/Low and rejection disagreements without using agreement as validation.','','The later native Gemini OpenKritt source workflow completed with zero finding records. No candidate means no eligible native deduplication, ranker or postprocessor model call; those calls are not reported as executed. Zero output is neither refutation nor proof of absence. Its three network failures and disclosed native queue resume remain preserved. The separately rejected OpenAI independent validator remains incomplete.','','The later Gemini Trail of Bits report supplies a logged paused-prize mock test but also contains source claims corrected in AQ-009. Its recipient test impersonates a contract that cannot originate redemption. Deliberately excluded tests and deployment tools cannot establish repository-wide absence. S5 raw arrays show 10 of 219 requirements checked and 209 unchecked, overriding its erroneous prose denominator. Native source correctness, workflow completion and transport success remain separate questions.','','The later scoped Gemini Simao and Pashov artifact seals support source observation reconciliation only. Simao native SUCCESS and Pashov strict ERROR are preserved. Both final independent method-semantic gates remain unchecked; this final source register does not qualify those native workflow cells. All raw IDs, numeric confidence values and disagreements remain visible.','','The pinned public-fork tests partially close real USDC/wrapper request compatibility for the recorded mainnet and Sepolia block hashes. They do not prove authentic off-chain VRF fulfillment, live candidate binding or future issuer/provider behavior. Initial skips, timeouts, compatibility adaptations and limited mutation/property domains remain in their original tool ledgers.','','## Remediation and re-audit order','','1. Decide and enforce the prize trust model. Any delivery-linked payout or fallback must account for all pre-settlement and settled liabilities, refunds, already delivered prizes and already paid claims. A dishonest NFT getter cannot establish truthfulness; a payment gate alone is insufficient. The earlier broken Option C is not a ready patch.','2. Address the narrow sponsor-return destination hazard and recipient capabilities with an explicit policy. Test sponsor-selected future clone addresses, actual contract callers and both quote/NFT terminal exits; retain atomic failure behavior.','3. Verify immutable deployment inputs, actual bytecode and constructor arguments, quote-token identity and supported wrapper behavior on the intended deployment. Separate pinned local-fork compatibility from live provider fulfillment.','4. Review documented dependency/configuration risks and marketplace assumptions, including fixed issuer-frozen recipients, unsupported fee/rebase quotes, stale marketplace orders and donations outside liabilities. Do not treat these as accepted by the owner.','5. Repair assurance gaps with reachable multi-actor handlers, non-vacuous action accounting, meaningful independent reference math, real callable recipient paths and mutation survival review. Re-run relevant tests and symbolic obligations on any authorized revision, without presenting bounded mocks as universal proofs.','','## Provenance and retained limits','','Every late report was read for findings only after its seal and target binding verified. Fresh cold controllers were not fed reconciliation, history or peer findings. Post-seal review and historical comparison are explicitly separate from those initial passes. No production source edits, deployments or live transactions were performed by reconciliation. Actual OpenAI rejections are preserved separately from Anthropic/Gemini outcomes and from 15-cell completion counts; no rejected request was retried or rephrased.','','No owner acceptance is requested or inferred. This file and register supersede earlier reconciliation snapshots for reading only. Root-owned final matrix, report and complete-package verification are separate responsibilities. The root coordinator received an actual OpenAI cybersecurity-risk rejection; it was not retried or replaced, and complete global delivery must not be inferred from this reconciliation.','','## Late reconciliation receipts','']
